1
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:29,260
Hey!

2
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:31,100
Singh! You should run away. Go!

3
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:31,780
Go!

4
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:33,940
This case is complicated.
You'll be screwed over!

5
00:00:34,210 --> 00:00:35,220
Run!

6
00:00:35,510 --> 00:00:36,180
Go!

7
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:06,740
I'm looking for someone.

8
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:10,460
The first one with the water element,
I already found him.

9
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:15,340
The second one with the wind element,
I think I'll find soon.

10
00:01:15,590 --> 00:01:17,420
The third one,

11
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:19,420
earth element.

12
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:26,700
The one known as the legendary
demon-slaying Necromancer.

13
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:13,940
Where is he?

14
00:02:14,430 --> 00:02:16,220
- I don't know.
- Hmm? Say that again.

15
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:21,820
I don't know.

16
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:25,420
Even if I knew,

17
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,700
I wouldn't tell you.

18
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:43,300
This family.

19
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:49,740
Let's talk later.

20
00:02:52,390 --> 00:02:53,980
We should wait for
the whole family to come home.

21
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:58,300
And don't bother running anywhere.

22
00:02:59,230 --> 00:03:00,220
You can't escape me.

23
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,140
(How to Enchant a Magic Knife)

24
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:03,780
Damn it!

25
00:04:05,310 --> 00:04:06,780
These are all amateurs!

26
00:04:07,710 --> 00:04:09,500
Some matters you really
have to do yourself!

27
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:16,180
This guy want this?

28
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,940
That guy want that?

29
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,980
Can't rely on anyone.

30
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:23,460
You'll see.

31
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:25,340
Gott.

32
00:05:05,030 --> 00:05:05,740
Min.

33
00:05:09,190 --> 00:05:10,860
Can we still call you Nam like before?

34
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:12,540
When I call you Min,

35
00:05:13,190 --> 00:05:14,140
it feels weird.

36
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,220
Just call me whatever.

37
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:19,260
Actually, if anyone calls me Min now,

38
00:05:19,410 --> 00:05:20,580
I won't even turn around.

39
00:05:27,990 --> 00:05:28,940
I think

40
00:05:29,510 --> 00:05:31,140
we need to end this ourselves.

41
00:05:34,730 --> 00:05:35,740
What will you do?

42
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:40,060
Go face Gott directly.

43
00:05:41,030 --> 00:05:41,940
Or...

44
00:05:42,790 --> 00:05:44,020
we run as far as we can.

45
00:05:46,390 --> 00:05:49,380
However far we run, he'll still find us.

46
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,380
Gott,

47
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:55,100
he's like karma.

48
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:56,940
Following us everywhere.

49
00:05:59,030 --> 00:06:00,340
But the worst thing is,

50
00:06:01,090 --> 00:06:03,100
he has the Satra Sutra book.

51
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:05,060
That's the interesting part.

52
00:06:23,590 --> 00:06:25,060
Or the answer is

53
00:06:28,690 --> 00:06:29,980
the Satra Sutra book.

54
00:06:38,430 --> 00:06:39,460
What do we do next?

55
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:44,140
Haven't thought about it yet.

56
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:48,460
Yeah.

57
00:07:22,130 --> 00:07:23,820
Hello. Auntie.

58
00:07:24,390 --> 00:07:25,900
I'm Wanchai, number two.

59
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:28,580
Please vote for number two.

60
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:29,500
Okay!

61
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:30,780
Thank you very much.

62
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:33,700
Ah! Uncle, Auntie, hello.

63
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,820
Please vote for number two. I'm Wanchai.

64
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:37,300
- Yes.
- Can you manage?

65
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,500
Number one is clearly leading.

66
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:42,260
For this district,
Rachine will win for sure.

67
00:07:42,590 --> 00:07:43,820
- It's not certain.
- Hm.

68
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,420
This party is popular too.

69
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:47,380
I asked people around my house.

70
00:07:47,590 --> 00:07:49,100
They're voting for number two.

71
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:52,340
This election will be intense for sure.

72
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:53,540
I guess so.

73
00:07:53,990 --> 00:07:55,740
Yeah, but how much are they
paying per vote?

74
00:07:55,910 --> 00:07:58,740
No one knows our local problems
better than our own people, Uncle.

75
00:07:59,130 --> 00:08:00,580
Please support me.

76
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:01,780
Thank you very much.

77
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:02,740
Hope you win!

78
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:05,220
Thank you very much, Uncle, Auntie.

79
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:08,100
- Please vote for number two.
- Okay!

80
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,940
Please support us.

81
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,300
- Number two.
- Number two.

82
00:08:17,770 --> 00:08:20,380
Yeah, yeah, you open the shop.
Just like normal, Foon.

83
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:23,340
Wait till things settle down,
then I'll go back.

84
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:25,460
I'm not worried about the cops.

85
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:27,780
Just worried about those guys.

86
00:08:29,330 --> 00:08:30,020
<i>Yeah.</i>

87
00:08:30,410 --> 00:08:32,060
You take good care of yourself.

88
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:04,380
You're bleeding.

89
00:09:04,810 --> 00:09:05,780
Is it a wound?

90
00:09:08,110 --> 00:09:10,100
Old wound. Never mind.

91
00:09:15,610 --> 00:09:18,140
How can I not mind?
Let me see so I can dress it.

92
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,500
Ow! It's okay!

93
00:09:29,930 --> 00:09:31,020
It's not okay!

94
00:09:31,110 --> 00:09:34,060
If you leave it like this,
you'll get infected with tetanus!

95
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:37,580
Do you want to get a fever
and go to the hospital?

96
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:41,340
If you don't dress it,
the blood won't stop flowing.

97
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:43,100
I have to dress it.

98
00:09:43,330 --> 00:09:44,300
It's just a little wound.

99
00:09:45,390 --> 00:09:46,980
It's not a little. It's very deep.

100
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:54,260
You have to dress it.
Or the bleeding won't stop.

101
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:57,060
Wait.

102
00:09:57,310 --> 00:09:59,100
- I'll go buy something.
- It's okay.

103
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:00,660
I'll go buy medicine to dress your wound.

104
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:02,700
Wait here. Just a minute.

105
00:10:17,190 --> 00:10:19,380
You got the enchantment.
Doesn't it work anymore?

106
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,500
Maybe the protection's worn off.

107
00:10:37,230 --> 00:10:38,260
You know what?

108
00:10:40,930 --> 00:10:44,300
When I was a kid,
I never had a good night's sleep.

109
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:52,180
When I grew up,

110
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:56,420
I never thought about the future.

111
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:00,300
Just

112
00:11:01,030 --> 00:11:02,300
lived day by day.

113
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,780
But later I started thinking.

114
00:11:16,590 --> 00:11:18,700
How I would take care of the people I love.

115
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:41,860
I've killed someone.

116
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:48,100
But I didn't mean to.

117
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:52,940
I...

118
00:11:53,690 --> 00:11:54,860
I'm sorry.

119
00:12:06,490 --> 00:12:07,740
I'm sorry too.

120
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:26,140
Don't feel sorry alone anymore.

121
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:31,020
You still have me, you know.

122
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:40,380
I can take care of you, Nam.

123
00:13:42,990 --> 00:13:43,940
Back then,

124
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:45,740
Mom wasn't home.

125
00:13:49,410 --> 00:13:51,380
My stepfather tried to rape me.

126
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,740
I refused.

127
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,300
I grabbed scissors.

128
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:06,140
So I stabbed him in the eye.

129
00:14:09,810 --> 00:14:10,900
He died.

130
00:14:16,630 --> 00:14:17,540
But

131
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,780
when Mom came home,

132
00:14:25,910 --> 00:14:27,780
Mom just scolded me on and on.

133
00:14:31,690 --> 00:14:32,700
She said...

134
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:36,500
she'd turn me in to the police.

135
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:43,820
So I ran to my uncle

136
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:46,620
who was guarding a casino in Chonburi.

137
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:54,020
Ran into the underworld.

138
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,860
No identity.

139
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:02,660
When someone told me to do something,

140
00:15:03,410 --> 00:15:04,460
I did as they said.

141
00:15:06,510 --> 00:15:08,500
When someone told me to kill someone,

142
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:11,100
I killed them.

143
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:17,620
No one could catch me.

144
00:15:18,910 --> 00:15:20,500
Because I had no identity.

145
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:25,060
You're lucky.

146
00:15:26,290 --> 00:15:27,660
You still have a father,

147
00:15:28,110 --> 00:15:29,140
a mother,

148
00:15:29,910 --> 00:15:31,140
and friends.

149
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:35,300
And I have you too.

150
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:58,220
Look. Where is it?

151
00:15:58,730 --> 00:16:00,620
- Ow!
- Damn, be careful!

152
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,380
If I win the lottery,
I'll replace this with a sofa.

153
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:04,260
- Do it then!
- Damn it!

154
00:16:04,510 --> 00:16:05,620
So hard to unfold.

155
00:16:06,110 --> 00:16:08,140
- Damn!
- Ow! Sad life!

156
00:16:08,310 --> 00:16:09,660
Hey! Ah!

157
00:16:09,770 --> 00:16:11,260
- How is it?
- Damn it!

158
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:13,700
Ow!

159
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:15,540
Pinching my finger every day!

160
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:18,340
I come to apologize to you guys.

161
00:16:33,790 --> 00:16:35,140
No need to apologize to us.

162
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:38,180
We have no value in society anyway.

163
00:16:38,930 --> 00:16:40,060
Especially to cops.

164
00:16:40,910 --> 00:16:44,580
We're just thugs, drug dealers,

165
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:46,260
people with no future.

166
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:48,900
Hey!

167
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:51,780
But I don't think of you guys like that.

168
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:54,100
I'm here to apologize.

169
00:16:56,640 --> 00:17:00,100
Yeah, yeah. At first,
I just wanted to investigate.

170
00:17:01,090 --> 00:17:02,580
But as time went on,

171
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:05,380
I thought you guys were real friends.

172
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:06,820
Hmm.

173
00:17:07,810 --> 00:17:08,620
Friends?

174
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:10,980
Friends don't do this to each other.

175
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:14,780
Even though we all
might not seem valuable,

176
00:17:15,340 --> 00:17:17,140
we love everyone sincerely.

177
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,860
Joe.

178
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,020
I'm sorry.

179
00:17:22,810 --> 00:17:24,380
No, Officer.

180
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:27,540
Keep your apology.
Tell them to Singh instead.

181
00:17:30,710 --> 00:17:31,460
Can I...

182
00:17:31,990 --> 00:17:33,740
ask you to apologize to Singh for me?

183
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:41,660
Actually, you don't need
to apologize to Singh.

184
00:17:42,390 --> 00:17:44,660
Singh already knew you were a cop.

185
00:17:45,930 --> 00:17:47,580
He's been in Pattaya for years.

186
00:17:47,890 --> 00:17:49,380
Hanging with these people.

187
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:52,180
At first glance,
he knows who's undercover,

188
00:17:52,340 --> 00:17:54,820
who's a dealer. Ghost sees ghost.

189
00:17:57,510 --> 00:17:58,180
Oh!

190
00:17:58,930 --> 00:17:59,660
Yeah.

191
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:00,980
He knew.

192
00:18:05,060 --> 00:18:06,180
And you came here,

193
00:18:07,930 --> 00:18:11,220
won't you buy us a bottle or two?

194
00:18:11,530 --> 00:18:12,220
Huh?

195
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:14,140
One!

196
00:18:14,430 --> 00:18:16,940
- Whoa!
- Go home with your one bottle.

197
00:18:17,510 --> 00:18:18,340
Two!

198
00:18:20,210 --> 00:18:20,820
Three!

199
00:18:21,010 --> 00:18:22,500
Yeah, yeah! Like this is good.

200
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,260
If it's about drinks, I forgive you.

201
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:26,460
Go!

202
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:28,180
- One arm can still help.
- Okay!

203
00:18:29,410 --> 00:18:31,540
- Where do you move them?
- Not a single normal body here.

204
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:33,580
- Hand hurts, arm broken.
- You're perfectly fine!

205
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:34,620
Which way?

206
00:18:34,730 --> 00:18:36,700
Soon you'll go blind, Foon!

207
00:19:05,010 --> 00:19:05,660
Hey!

208
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:08,860
What do you want?

209
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:11,540
Why are you following me?

210
00:19:20,210 --> 00:19:22,620
If Rachine doesn't run,

211
00:19:27,430 --> 00:19:28,700
will anyone replace him?

212
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:40,420
Me.

213
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:42,500
Put me in.

214
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:44,500
But

215
00:19:45,710 --> 00:19:47,340
I might not win.

216
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:51,060
Rachine has a strong existing base.

217
00:19:51,660 --> 00:19:53,660
If you put in a new person,
I think it's hard.

218
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:56,580
Number two is also strong.

219
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:58,980
But if I run, I'll win.

220
00:20:00,730 --> 00:20:01,500
Really.

221
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,580
Are you listening?

222
00:20:10,690 --> 00:20:12,300
You're that confident?

223
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:18,100
Yeah.

224
00:20:21,030 --> 00:20:24,100
Well, if you're confident,
you have to win if you run, right?

225
00:20:24,310 --> 00:20:25,500
Of course!

226
00:20:25,910 --> 00:20:27,060
Of fucking course!

227
00:20:28,030 --> 00:20:29,740
Village headman, SAO, PAO,

228
00:20:29,890 --> 00:20:31,100
all the same group.

229
00:20:32,510 --> 00:20:33,420
Trust me.

230
00:20:34,010 --> 00:20:34,820
Really.

231
00:22:57,700 --> 00:22:59,900
- Hello.
- Hello, beautiful auntie.

232
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:01,500
I'm Wanchai, number two.

233
00:23:01,610 --> 00:23:03,500
Please vote for number two.

234
00:23:03,940 --> 00:23:05,460
Hello. Thank you very much.

235
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:18,980
Hey!

236
00:23:23,090 --> 00:23:23,940
Who did this?

237
00:23:25,190 --> 00:23:27,140
Who ordered the hit
on number two, Wanchai?

238
00:23:28,180 --> 00:23:29,340
Who was hired?

239
00:23:32,660 --> 00:23:34,420
There's no one else. Just us.

240
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:37,580
What? Is there someone else?

241
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:42,180
Right now, only two people are running.
Me and him.

242
00:23:42,390 --> 00:23:43,500
Who ordered the hit?

243
00:23:44,330 --> 00:23:46,060
Is someone else trying to
compete with me?

244
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:47,500
Me.

245
00:24:37,660 --> 00:24:38,460
You.

246
00:24:47,980 --> 00:24:49,980
I'll make you an offer.

247
00:24:55,680 --> 00:24:56,900
You'll get...

248
00:24:57,380 --> 00:24:58,300
power.

249
00:24:59,110 --> 00:25:00,820
You'll get success.

250
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:05,100
But you must do everything I say.

251
00:25:10,330 --> 00:25:12,020
In exchange for your breath.

252
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:15,220
Hmm?

253
00:25:20,210 --> 00:25:21,020
Yeah.

254
00:25:30,430 --> 00:25:31,940
Did you make a deal with him?

255
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:33,740
So it would...

256
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:37,100
extend your life?

257
00:25:38,330 --> 00:25:39,620
If it were you, what would you do?

258
00:25:40,730 --> 00:25:42,900
I know you want to run for MP against me.

259
00:25:43,510 --> 00:25:44,540
Dream on.

260
00:25:45,460 --> 00:25:47,620
You think you'll win if you compete?

261
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:49,940
People will still vote for me.

262
00:25:50,380 --> 00:25:51,780
How much money have I spent?

263
00:25:52,180 --> 00:25:53,740
You're going to swoop in?

264
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:55,900
Who would vote for you?

265
00:25:56,540 --> 00:25:57,340
Yeah.

266
00:25:58,840 --> 00:26:00,860
What you said is true.

267
00:26:02,860 --> 00:26:05,100
Running doesn't mean you'll win.

268
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:08,780
Winning over the whole province is hard.

269
00:26:09,140 --> 00:26:10,860
Another thing, this game,

270
00:26:13,630 --> 00:26:15,020
you're not a player.

271
00:26:15,910 --> 00:26:17,020
You must understand.

272
00:26:28,460 --> 00:26:29,380
Rachine,

273
00:26:30,910 --> 00:26:32,020
you didn't think it through.

274
00:26:33,580 --> 00:26:36,820
Soon he will come to reclaim
both your life and your breath!

275
00:26:37,410 --> 00:26:38,260
Fool!

276
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:48,820
He's telling the truth.

277
00:27:49,790 --> 00:27:51,940
You owe them a lot of money, right?

278
00:27:53,730 --> 00:27:55,380
I want to help.

279
00:28:07,210 --> 00:28:08,340
Wow.

280
00:28:15,680 --> 00:28:16,660
Umami.

281
00:28:29,080 --> 00:28:29,820
Hey!

282
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:32,180
Tomorrow you have to pay 400,000.

283
00:28:32,680 --> 00:28:34,020
You've put me off many times.

284
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:35,220
Go find it.

285
00:28:36,210 --> 00:28:37,580
If you don't pay tomorrow,

286
00:28:37,960 --> 00:28:39,340
at your house in the evening,

287
00:28:39,580 --> 00:28:41,060
you can eat lead for dinner.

288
00:28:41,490 --> 00:28:42,380
Oh, brother!

289
00:28:42,740 --> 00:28:43,780
Calm down, brother.

290
00:28:43,940 --> 00:28:45,940
Tomorrow I'll definitely get
you the money, brother.

291
00:28:46,140 --> 00:28:47,620
Don't worry, brother.
Because soon...

292
00:28:50,780 --> 00:28:51,540
Bastard!

293
00:28:52,240 --> 00:28:53,460
Damn pushy!

294
00:28:53,610 --> 00:28:54,620
Do I have it, you bastard?

295
00:28:54,760 --> 00:28:57,820
So damn pushy!
If I see him, I'll slap his face.

296
00:28:57,950 --> 00:28:59,020
What a prick!

297
00:30:12,140 --> 00:30:13,860
Whoa, so late! I thought he's dead.

298
00:30:14,010 --> 00:30:15,700
Does he see us? Does he?

299
00:30:16,140 --> 00:30:17,180
Not yet.

300
00:30:22,340 --> 00:30:23,060
Here, Uncle.

301
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:24,100
Thank you.

302
00:30:24,680 --> 00:30:25,460
Singh!

303
00:30:26,040 --> 00:30:27,220
How did you get here?

304
00:30:27,610 --> 00:30:29,140
- Why did you come back?
- I came to get something.

305
00:30:29,250 --> 00:30:31,220
- Damn it!
- The cops will come for you!

306
00:30:32,440 --> 00:30:33,060
Singh!

307
00:30:33,610 --> 00:30:35,460
Damn, what is with you?
Not talking to me?

308
00:30:36,510 --> 00:30:38,020
- Singh!
- Where are you rushing off to?

309
00:30:39,210 --> 00:30:39,900
Hey!

310
00:30:43,060 --> 00:30:44,460
What did that bastard go in to get?

311
00:30:52,340 --> 00:30:53,100
Singh!

312
00:30:56,380 --> 00:30:59,180
By the way, I brought free
concert tickets for Joe and Foon.

313
00:30:59,390 --> 00:31:00,580
Foon asked for it.

314
00:31:01,880 --> 00:31:03,740
And I apologize to you too.

315
00:31:04,080 --> 00:31:05,220
Sorry about everything.

316
00:31:05,410 --> 00:31:06,860
- I thought you were a real friend...
- Yeah.

317
00:31:07,780 --> 00:31:08,540
It's okay.

318
00:31:09,240 --> 00:31:09,980
Never mind.

319
00:31:10,630 --> 00:31:12,260
I told you
he doesn't think anything of it.

320
00:31:12,490 --> 00:31:13,140
Yeah.

321
00:31:14,310 --> 00:31:15,100
Hey, Singh!

322
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:16,660
What about Nam?

323
00:31:19,540 --> 00:31:20,380
I don't know.

324
00:31:20,940 --> 00:31:22,380
My motorcycle's gone too.

325
00:31:24,540 --> 00:31:25,940
Where is she?

326
00:31:28,380 --> 00:31:29,620
I'm worried she's in danger.

327
00:31:30,180 --> 00:31:31,140
I don't know.

328
00:31:31,690 --> 00:31:33,260
Nam took your motorcycle, right?

329
00:31:33,840 --> 00:31:34,500
Yeah.

330
00:31:54,540 --> 00:31:55,580
Falling every day.

331
00:31:56,280 --> 00:31:57,580
And I have to sweep every day.

332
00:31:57,690 --> 00:31:59,820
Is there ever a day they don't fall?
Just one day?

333
00:32:10,340 --> 00:32:11,460
Oh, what are you doing, Singh?

334
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:12,540
Hello, Teacher.

335
00:32:13,110 --> 00:32:14,140
What?

336
00:32:14,480 --> 00:32:16,140
Hey! These days, so arrogant.

337
00:32:16,360 --> 00:32:17,580
Walking pass me without a chat.

338
00:32:17,860 --> 00:32:19,700
Runs straight into the temple hall.

339
00:32:42,790 --> 00:32:43,580
Oh, that...

340
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:47,460
Leaves without saying goodbye.
With your large jacket.

341
00:32:48,140 --> 00:32:49,340
Hey! Or did Singh...

342
00:32:49,610 --> 00:32:50,700
Hey! Thief!

343
00:32:50,930 --> 00:32:52,580
Singh! Hey! Come back and talk first!

344
00:32:52,710 --> 00:32:53,300
Hey!

345
00:32:54,440 --> 00:32:55,980
Damn, Singh!

346
00:32:56,140 --> 00:32:57,460
What is with him?

347
00:33:39,540 --> 00:33:40,220
Hey!

348
00:34:28,930 --> 00:34:29,740
Hey!

349
00:35:01,180 --> 00:35:02,020
Why did you follow me?

350
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:05,540
I'm worried.

351
00:35:05,880 --> 00:35:06,980
Why did you come here?

352
00:35:09,900 --> 00:35:11,060
To get the book.

353
00:35:11,510 --> 00:35:13,100
In case it can end everything.

354
00:35:14,140 --> 00:35:15,180
Are you hurt?

355
00:35:16,340 --> 00:35:17,300
Got hit too.

356
00:35:17,540 --> 00:35:18,700
Asking if I'm hurt?

357
00:35:19,080 --> 00:35:20,220
I'm just asking nicely.

358
00:35:42,780 --> 00:35:44,700
Yeah. Both of you came.

359
00:35:48,790 --> 00:35:50,940
You're just like your father.

360
00:35:52,560 --> 00:35:54,300
Evil truly runs in the blood.

361
00:35:54,680 --> 00:35:56,700
I don't know what the hell
you're talking about.

362
00:35:57,680 --> 00:35:59,180
Don't mess with my family!

363
00:36:00,510 --> 00:36:01,260
Power.

364
00:36:02,180 --> 00:36:03,060
Authority.

365
00:36:05,380 --> 00:36:07,140
Does it feel good to have it?

366
00:36:10,740 --> 00:36:11,460
No.

367
00:36:12,560 --> 00:36:13,900
Won't feel good much longer.

368
00:36:14,170 --> 00:36:15,580
Because soon I'll take it back.

369
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:17,140
It's me

370
00:36:17,490 --> 00:36:18,820
that will take everything back.

371
00:37:10,580 --> 00:37:11,300
Nam!

372
00:37:15,180 --> 00:37:16,180
Nam! Let go!

373
00:37:16,510 --> 00:37:17,140
Nam!

374
00:37:18,940 --> 00:37:19,660
Let me go!

375
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:38,060
Go, Nam!

376
00:38:10,950 --> 00:38:11,820
Yes.

377
00:38:13,980 --> 00:38:15,900
The one with the wind element.

378
00:38:18,100 --> 00:38:21,380
Just one more left.
The one with the earth element.

379
00:39:01,640 --> 00:39:03,340
Five, seven, three.

380
00:39:08,540 --> 00:39:10,500
Trust me and you'll survive.

381
00:39:13,710 --> 00:39:16,300
Bring me betel leaves and rice.

382
00:39:40,010 --> 00:39:41,100
Done!

383
00:39:42,640 --> 00:39:43,220
Ow!

384
00:39:43,440 --> 00:39:44,500
Lottery results, results!

385
00:39:48,880 --> 00:39:49,740
It's time!

386
00:40:08,330 --> 00:40:10,100
Why did this number come out?

387
00:40:11,080 --> 00:40:11,820
Auntie!

388
00:40:12,980 --> 00:40:14,300
What was the winning three number?

389
00:40:15,240 --> 00:40:16,940
Five, seven, three!

390
00:40:20,380 --> 00:40:22,220
What the hell is this?

391
00:40:24,890 --> 00:40:26,060
Seven, five, seven.

392
00:40:26,410 --> 00:40:28,300
Three, seven, eight.
What the hell did I buy?

393
00:40:28,620 --> 00:40:29,780
Five, seven, three!

394
00:40:31,480 --> 00:40:32,780
1000 x 1000!

395
00:40:34,480 --> 00:40:35,820
500,000!

396
00:40:36,380 --> 00:40:38,540
Damn! 500,000!

397
00:40:43,180 --> 00:40:45,740
Damn it! 500,000!

398
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:48,740
- Damn!
- What's happening to me?

399
00:40:49,110 --> 00:40:50,500
Lose every time!

400
00:40:52,760 --> 00:40:53,420
Auntie!

401
00:40:54,850 --> 00:40:56,460
- What?
- How much do I owe for food?

402
00:40:56,860 --> 00:40:59,020
- 4,590.
- Oh!

403
00:41:00,530 --> 00:41:01,380
Come here!

404
00:41:02,230 --> 00:41:03,220
- Come here!
- Huh?

405
00:41:04,090 --> 00:41:05,860
Scan it quick, quick!

406
00:41:06,390 --> 00:41:07,220
Quick!

407
00:41:07,920 --> 00:41:09,860
- Huh?
- Here, 5,000. Scan it first!

408
00:41:11,230 --> 00:41:14,380
- Yeah, no change needed!
- Hey! Actually 5,000!

409
00:41:16,630 --> 00:41:17,660
Why are you confused?

410
00:41:21,430 --> 00:41:23,540
Boss Danai! Whoa!

411
00:41:23,780 --> 00:41:27,140
- Whoa, Boss Danai!
- Amazing!

412
00:41:27,380 --> 00:41:28,620
Poseidon!

413
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:30,420
Man United!

414
00:41:31,020 --> 00:41:32,940
I'm going to conquer all today!

415
00:41:33,060 --> 00:41:34,810
I'm telling you,
I've been holding back inside!

416
00:41:35,010 --> 00:41:35,940
Ah, whoa!

417
00:41:36,140 --> 00:41:36,820
Hey!

418
00:41:37,510 --> 00:41:38,140
Hey!

419
00:41:38,740 --> 00:41:39,980
Come get your money right now!

420
00:41:40,280 --> 00:41:41,460
Don't wait till evening!

421
00:41:41,980 --> 00:41:43,660
Hey! Yeah, tonight!

422
00:41:43,980 --> 00:41:46,980
I'm betting on Man United this match!
Going all in!

423
00:41:47,780 --> 00:41:49,140
See you tonight!

424
00:41:49,410 --> 00:41:50,140
Okay!

425
00:41:56,160 --> 00:41:57,020
Damn!

426
00:41:57,780 --> 00:42:00,060
People with money
are so cool doing anything!

427
00:42:03,410 --> 00:42:04,740
Please support me.

428
00:42:04,980 --> 00:42:07,220
Rachine, number one. Thank you.

429
00:42:07,610 --> 00:42:08,820
Please support me.

430
00:42:09,010 --> 00:42:11,380
Same party! Oh, hello, hello!

431
00:42:11,880 --> 00:42:13,220
Oh, here's a sign too.

432
00:42:14,610 --> 00:42:16,820
Yes, Rachine, number one.
Don't forget!

433
00:42:17,440 --> 00:42:18,220
Yeah.

434
00:42:21,040 --> 00:42:21,700
Inspector.

435
00:42:22,130 --> 00:42:24,220
Keep a close watch on
candidate number one, Mr. Rachine.

436
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:25,860
Strong competitors

437
00:42:26,030 --> 00:42:27,420
are withdrawing one by one.

438
00:42:27,640 --> 00:42:29,460
Number one is floating along alone.

439
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:31,780
And the drug smuggling case at the port,

440
00:42:32,330 --> 00:42:34,100
Mr. Rachine is probably involved too.

441
00:42:34,590 --> 00:42:36,580
Inspector, find more evidence for me.

442
00:42:36,840 --> 00:42:37,980
Yes, Lieutenant.

443
00:42:39,280 --> 00:42:39,940
Lieutenant.

444
00:42:40,240 --> 00:42:41,460
The Deputy is waiting to see you.

445
00:42:56,310 --> 00:42:57,100
Excuse me.

446
00:42:57,880 --> 00:42:58,660
Sit.

447
00:43:04,990 --> 00:43:07,220
Deputy, is there something urgent?

448
00:43:08,780 --> 00:43:10,140
Are there CCTV cameras?

449
00:43:12,540 --> 00:43:13,660
Shouldn't be any.

450
00:43:14,730 --> 00:43:15,820
It is urgent.

451
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:20,020
I heard there's an investigation
into the murder of MP Wanchai

452
00:43:20,240 --> 00:43:21,780
who was shot dead.

453
00:43:22,280 --> 00:43:25,340
And word is Mr. Rachine is
involved in this case too.

454
00:43:27,640 --> 00:43:29,620
The boss ordered it from above.

455
00:43:31,790 --> 00:43:34,580
He doesn't want Mr. Rachine
involved in this case.

456
00:43:41,330 --> 00:43:42,820
But from the leads we have,

457
00:43:43,110 --> 00:43:45,500
I think Mr. Rachine is
involved in this case.

458
00:43:46,240 --> 00:43:48,940
Right now I have my people
gathering more information.

459
00:43:52,230 --> 00:43:53,660
You're overthinking it.

460
00:43:57,210 --> 00:43:58,860
But from the information we have,

461
00:43:59,890 --> 00:44:02,260
many deaths were from local politics.

462
00:44:03,340 --> 00:44:05,980
And almost every case is
connected to Mr. Rachine.

463
00:44:06,460 --> 00:44:07,740
And in some cases,

464
00:44:08,640 --> 00:44:11,180
people saw Mr. Rachine
at the crime scene.

465
00:44:11,380 --> 00:44:12,780
Redo the case file.

466
00:44:14,110 --> 00:44:17,220
That case must not involve Mr. Rachin.

467
00:44:20,510 --> 00:44:22,180
Working here, you must understand.

468
00:44:23,180 --> 00:44:24,500
I don't want trouble.

469
00:44:25,290 --> 00:44:26,820
Neither do you, right?

470
00:44:37,160 --> 00:44:38,300
Please help me out.

471
00:44:38,810 --> 00:44:39,580
Yes, sir.

472
00:45:00,380 --> 00:45:02,140
I'll give you 30 million.

473
00:45:03,280 --> 00:45:05,340
The other 10 million,
I'll let the boys split.

474
00:45:05,840 --> 00:45:06,580
Are we good?

475
00:45:07,190 --> 00:45:10,300
Hey! I heard the area
has stubborn people.

476
00:45:10,640 --> 00:45:12,180
I have my boys cleared them out.

477
00:45:12,510 --> 00:45:13,740
No problem now.

478
00:45:15,140 --> 00:45:16,780
Hope there is no problem now.

479
00:45:17,740 --> 00:45:18,460
Okay.

480
00:45:18,730 --> 00:45:20,540
Sure. Talk to you later.

481
00:45:23,360 --> 00:45:24,140
Damn!

482
00:45:26,140 --> 00:45:28,580
Doing nothing all day.
No investment.

483
00:45:28,980 --> 00:45:32,300
Become a civil servant just to eat
every day, eat till they burst!

484
00:45:32,480 --> 00:45:33,460
Bastards!

485
00:45:34,080 --> 00:45:34,860
Damn!

486
00:45:36,930 --> 00:45:38,860
Sir, Mr. Anon is here to see you.

487
00:45:40,940 --> 00:45:41,780
Let him in.

488
00:45:49,110 --> 00:45:49,940
Come in.

489
00:45:52,640 --> 00:45:54,300
You still dare show your face?

490
00:45:55,040 --> 00:45:56,420
Many times now!

491
00:45:57,760 --> 00:45:59,300
Sir, I'm sorry.

492
00:46:00,290 --> 00:46:01,300
I'm really sorry, sir.

493
00:46:01,540 --> 00:46:02,980
I brought something to apologize.

494
00:46:03,190 --> 00:46:03,900
Here.

495
00:46:06,430 --> 00:46:08,180
I'm here to inform you that

496
00:46:08,730 --> 00:46:11,620
the other day some Russians
wanted to order a big batch from me.

497
00:46:12,030 --> 00:46:13,420
But I told them no.

498
00:46:13,590 --> 00:46:16,540
Big batches must be
Mr. Rachine's responsibility only.

499
00:46:19,240 --> 00:46:20,420
Of course!

500
00:46:20,880 --> 00:46:24,060
Who would trust you?
Backstabber! Damn it!

501
00:46:26,230 --> 00:46:28,380
Yes, sir. You're right.

502
00:46:29,040 --> 00:46:32,100
I have nothing to negotiate with you.
Can't compare to you at all.

503
00:46:32,480 --> 00:46:34,980
I could never match your prestige.

504
00:46:40,540 --> 00:46:42,020
Getting smarter now.

505
00:46:43,810 --> 00:46:44,580
Fine.

506
00:46:45,440 --> 00:46:47,060
But wait till I finish this batch first.

507
00:46:47,650 --> 00:46:50,580
Next batch, leave the Russian's number.
I'll contact them myself.

508
00:46:51,580 --> 00:46:52,620
Yes, yes.

509
00:46:54,640 --> 00:46:55,420
Thank you.

510
00:47:01,490 --> 00:47:02,260
Sir.

511
00:47:03,160 --> 00:47:04,460
You're very decisive.

512
00:47:05,050 --> 00:47:06,060
Wow! Amazing!

513
00:47:06,660 --> 00:47:09,620
You dared to trade your life
and breath with Gott.

514
00:47:10,940 --> 00:47:13,340
That means there was a good deal, right?

515
00:47:13,880 --> 00:47:15,140
What's so good about it?

516
00:47:17,140 --> 00:47:18,260
I survived.

517
00:47:19,690 --> 00:47:21,420
If I could find someone to deal with him,

518
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:23,260
I wouldn't keep him as my boss.

519
00:47:28,020 --> 00:47:29,260
I can handle it for you.

520
00:47:30,260 --> 00:47:31,620
Gott trusts me.

521
00:47:33,780 --> 00:47:35,180
Because if it wasn't for him, honestly,

522
00:47:35,270 --> 00:47:37,340
my business would be
much more prosperous.

523
00:47:38,940 --> 00:47:41,100
No one in this city would think I'm just...

524
00:47:41,580 --> 00:47:42,700
a show bar owner.

525
00:47:43,410 --> 00:47:45,300
I could do so much more for you.

526
00:47:47,210 --> 00:47:48,460
Handle it for me?

527
00:47:50,810 --> 00:47:52,340
A nobody like you?

528
00:47:55,580 --> 00:47:56,180
Hm.

529
00:47:57,260 --> 00:47:59,180
You're so pitiful.

530
00:48:00,080 --> 00:48:02,340
Running for MP. Want to be accepted.

531
00:48:02,680 --> 00:48:04,060
Who would vote for you?

532
00:48:05,620 --> 00:48:09,020
Even Gott knows.
Someone like you is pitiful. Fool!

533
00:48:17,260 --> 00:48:18,780
Damn Anon! Bastard!

534
00:48:24,310 --> 00:48:25,100
Fuck you!
